Q1_25 = [{"q":1,"topic":"Geography","stem":"Consider the following assertion:\nIn the Pleistocene period either the Yamuna once flowed into the Indus, or the Sutlej flowed into the Yamuna and one major tributary of either had shifted from the Ganga to the Indus or vice versa.\nWhich of the following is/are the basis of the above assertion?","statements":["The Nadi-Sukta of the Rigveda","The explorations of the Sutlej and the Yamuna by Robert Bruce Foote","The presence of the same species of dolphins in both the Indus and the Ganga river systems"],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 only","b":"2 only","c":"1 and 2","d":"3"},"answer":"d","reason":"Same Platanista dolphin species in both river systems indicates ancient hydrological connection.","confidence":"medium"},{"q":2,"topic":"Art & Culture","stem":"What does an empty seat represent in early Buddhist iconography?","statements":None,"select_prompt":"","options":{"a":"The meditation of the Buddha","b":"The Buddha's First Sermon","c":"The Buddha's Mahaparinibbana","d":"The Buddha's Mahabhinishkramana"},"answer":"a","reason":"In aniconic Buddhist art, the empty throne under the Bodhi tree symbolises the Buddha's presence and meditation.","confidence":"high"},{"q":3,"topic":"Ancient History","stem":"Which of the following pairs of ancient and modern names of rivers is/are correctly matched?","statements":["Vitasta : Chenab","Asikni : Jhelum","Parushni : Ravi","Vyavyati : Beas"],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 and 2","b":"3 and 4","c":"3 only","d":"4 only"},"answer":"c","reason":"Parushni = Ravi is correct. Vitasta = Jhelum, Asikni = Chenab (swapped); Vipasa = Beas (not Vyavyati).","confidence":"high"},{"q":4,"topic":"Art & Culture","stem":"Which of the following statements on the Amaravati Stupa and its relief sculpture is/are correct?","statements":["It was located in the lower Krishna valley.","In India, it was next only to the Sanchi Stupa in size.","The Amaravati school of sculpture made a lasting impact on the later South Indian sculpture, and its products were carried to Sri Lanka and South-east Asia."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 only","b":"1 and 3 only","c":"2 and 3 only","d":"1, 2 and 3"},"answer":"b","reason":"Amaravati was in lower Krishna valley and influenced South Indian, Sri Lankan and SE Asian art; it was the largest stupa, not second to Sanchi.","confidence":"high"},{"q":5,"topic":"Ancient History","stem":"Which of the following pairs of the king and his dynasty in early historical Tamilakam is/are not correctly matched?","statements":["Senguttuvan : Chera","Udiyanjeral : Chola","Nedunjeliyan : Pandya"],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 and 2","b":"2 only","c":"1 and 3","d":"3 only"},"answer":"b","reason":"Udiyanjeral was a Chera king, not Chola. The other two pairs are correct.","confidence":"high"},{"q":6,"topic":"Modern History","stem":"Which of the following factors contributed to the formation of the Forward Bloc by Subhas Chandra Bose in 1939?","statements":["Bose failed to win the confidence of Mahatma Gandhi.","The Congress Left was disunited and failed to support Bose.","The Communists did not support Bose in his endeavours.","The supporters of M.N. Roy and socialist leaders like Jayaprakash Narayan preferred Congress unity to supporting Bose."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1, 2 and 3","b":"1, 2 and 4","c":"1, 3 and 4","d":"2 and 4 only"},"answer":"b","reason":"Bose lost Gandhi's confidence; Congress Left was divided; Roy/JP socialists chose Congress unity. Communists initially supported Bose.","confidence":"medium"},{"q":7,"topic":"Modern History","stem":"Consider the following statements regarding the British policy in Awadh immediately after its annexation in 1856:","statements":["The taluqdars were dispossessed of their estates but allowed to retain their arms and forts.","A Summary Revenue Settlement was made in 1856 assuming that the taluqdars were outsiders.","The British believed in taking revenue directly from the peasants by removing the taluqdars."],"select_prompt":"Which of the statements given above is/are correct?","options":{"a":"2 and 3 only","b":"1 and 3 only","c":"1, 2 and 3","d":"2 only"},"answer":"a","reason":"Taluqdars were dispossessed AND disarmed (so 1 is wrong); Summary Settlement bypassed them to deal directly with peasants.","confidence":"high"},{"q":8,"topic":"Modern History","stem":"Consider the following assertion:\nThe genesis of political alliances based on community lay in the very nature of the Montague-Chelmsford Reforms, 1919.\nWhich of the following statements support/supports the above assertion?","statements":["Reforms retained and extended the principle of separate electorates.","Separate electorates were supposed to counter Indian nationalism, which was growing stronger.","Deprived classes rallied around the favours inherent in separate electorates."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 only","b":"2 and 3 only","c":"1 and 2 only","d":"1, 2 and 3"},"answer":"d","reason":"Montford retained and extended separate electorates to weaken nationalism and accommodate depressed classes — institutionalising communal politics.","confidence":"high"},{"q":9,"topic":"Art & Culture","stem":"Pandit Mallikarjun Mansur, the famous classical singer from Karnataka, represented the:","statements":None,"select_prompt":"","options":{"a":"Agra Gharana","b":"Gwalior Gharana","c":"Patiala Gharana","d":"Jaipur-Atrauli Gharana"},"answer":"d","reason":"Mallikarjun Mansur of Dharwad was a renowned exponent of the Jaipur-Atrauli gharana founded by Alladiya Khan.","confidence":"high"},{"q":10,"topic":"Ancient History","stem":"In which one among the following texts does the term kshetra-patni ('mistress of the field') originate?","statements":None,"select_prompt":"","options":{"a":"Rigveda","b":"Atharvaveda","c":"Ashtadhyayi","d":"Arthashastra"},"answer":"b","reason":"The term kshetra-patni occurs in the Atharvaveda in hymns linked to agricultural rituals.","confidence":"medium"},{"q":11,"topic":"Art & Culture","stem":"Which one of the following Carnatic music ragas is similar to Raga Bilawal in Hindustani music?","statements":None,"select_prompt":"","options":{"a":"Nat Bhairavi","b":"Kamavardhini","c":"Hanumatodi","d":"Dheera Shankarabharanam"},"answer":"d","reason":"Dheera Shankarabharanam (29th melakarta) uses the natural major scale identical to Bilawal thaat.","confidence":"high"},{"q":12,"topic":"Modern History","stem":"The artificially fixed rupee-sterling exchange rate prescribed by the Hilton-Young Commission (1926) was adopted by the British Government for which one of the following reasons?","statements":None,"select_prompt":"","options":{"a":"Aiding the flow of remittances from India and maintaining India's creditworthiness","b":"Providing support to Indian importers","c":"Encouraging export of cotton produce from India","d":"Preventing depreciation of the Rupee in terms of gold"},"answer":"a","reason":"The high 1s 6d rate aided sterling Home Charges remittances from India and safeguarded India's external creditworthiness for British interests.","confidence":"high"},{"q":13,"topic":"Ancient History","stem":"Consider the following statements:","statements":["Pali texts contain the first definite references to coins, e.g., kahapana, nikkha, kamsa, and kakanika.","The literary evidence from Pali texts is corroborated by archaeological evidence of punch-marked coins from many sites, most of them made of silver."],"select_prompt":"The above statements have been associated with which of the following?\n1. Emergence of urban life\n2. Transition to money economy\nSelect the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 only","b":"2 only","c":"Both 1 and 2","d":"Neither 1 nor 2"},"answer":"c","reason":"Together they indicate both Second Urbanisation (emergence of urban life) and the transition to a money-based economy.","confidence":"high"},{"q":14,"topic":"Art & Culture","stem":"Which of the following temples has/have a Nagara-style shikhara?","statements":["Malegitti Shivalaya, Badami","Huchimalligudi Temple, Aihole","Dashavatara Temple, Deogarh","Virupaksha Temple, Pattadakal"],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 and 2","b":"2 and 3","c":"3 only","d":"3 and 4"},"answer":"c","reason":"Only Dashavatara Temple at Deogarh has a Nagara shikhara; Badami/Aihole/Pattadakal Virupaksha are Dravidian.","confidence":"medium"},{"q":15,"topic":"Art & Culture","stem":"Among the four main forms of existence of life recognized in Jainism, which one of the following is not included?","statements":None,"select_prompt":"","options":{"a":"Deva (gods)","b":"Yaksha (demi-gods)","c":"Manushya (humans)","d":"Tiryancha (animals and plants)"},"answer":"b","reason":"Jainism's four gatis are deva, manushya, tiryancha, and naraki (hell-beings); yaksha is not a separate category.","confidence":"high"},{"q":16,"topic":"Art & Culture","stem":"The Hallisalasya painting in the Bagh Caves represents:","statements":None,"select_prompt":"","options":{"a":"A joyous folk dance","b":"Buddha in a meditative pose","c":"The depiction of Shiva and Parvati on Kailasha","d":"Samudramanthan (Churning of the Ocean)"},"answer":"a","reason":"Bagh Cave 4's Hallisalasya panel depicts a circular folk dance with musicians.","confidence":"high"},{"q":17,"topic":"Ancient History","stem":"Consider the following statements relating to the use of the place-value system in India:","statements":["The earliest epigraphic use of the place-value system in India is found in the Mankani plates from Gujarat (AD 595 - 596).","In the ninth century, place-values become general in inscriptions all over India.","The place-values have been found in Sanskrit inscriptions in South-east Asia as early as the seventh century."],"select_prompt":"Which of the statements given above are correct?","options":{"a":"1 and 2 only","b":"1 and 3 only","c":"2 and 3 only","d":"1, 2 and 3"},"answer":"a","reason":"Mankani plates (595-596 AD) show earliest epigraphic place-value; it became general in 9th-century Indian inscriptions. SE Asian use started 8th century.","confidence":"medium"},{"q":18,"topic":"Ancient History","stem":"Consider the following statements about the archaeological findings in Harappan towns:","statements":["There is wide occurrence of spindle-whorls in the houses but absence of spinning wheels.","Weights and measurement scales, complete with graduations have been discovered.","There are houses built in large part with baked bricks, around relatively spacious courtyards, with their own wells, bathing platforms, and large rooms."],"select_prompt":"Which of the following inferences can be drawn from the above statements?\n1. Statement I suggests that spinning was a laborious activity done at home.\n2. Statement II suggests the extent of the scientific knowledge that the Harappans possessed.\n3. Statement III suggests the emergence of a common property system.\nSelect the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 and 2 only","b":"2 and 3 only","c":"1 and 3 only","d":"1, 2 and 3"},"answer":"a","reason":"Spindle-whorls without wheels imply laborious home spinning; graduated weights show scientific knowledge. Spacious private houses with own wells imply PRIVATE property, not common.","confidence":"medium"},{"q":19,"topic":"Modern History","stem":"Which one of the following statements about the Eka Movement and Bardoli Satyagraha is correct?","statements":None,"select_prompt":"","options":{"a":"The Eka Movement was throughout supported and organized by the Congress while Bardoli Satyagraha was initially independent of Congress influence and was only in the last stages supported by the Congress.","b":"The Eka Movement was provided leadership by the taluqdars of Awadh, whereas the Bardoli Satyagraha was a movement of the landless labourers.","c":"The Bardoli Satyagraha was a campaign against the enhancement of land revenue, while the Eka Movement was a protest against excessive extraction of rents.","d":"The Eka Movement was located in the Varanasi and Mirzapur districts of the present-day U.P., while the Bardoli Satyagraha took place in Saurashtra."},"answer":"c","reason":"Bardoli (1928) protested a 22% land-revenue hike; Eka (1921-22) in Hardoi/Sitapur opposed excessive rent extraction by taluqdars.","confidence":"high"},{"q":20,"topic":"Ancient History","stem":"Consider the following statements about the Rigvedic period:","statements":["Irrigation from wells allowed agriculture to expand away from flood plains and strips on river margins into the present Punjab and Haryana plains having underground water levels reasonably close to the surface.","Draught-animal power was employed to draw up water out of the wells."],"select_prompt":"Which of the following information support/supports the above statements?\n1. There is evidence in the Rigveda of the use of ashma chakra (stone pulley wheel) and ahava (strapped wooden pails) to draw up water.\n2. Mention has been made in the Rigveda of the use of implements like parashu / kulisha (axe) and datra / sreni (sickle).\n3. There is a history of the use of ox, even before the Rigveda, for ploughing the land and pulling the carts.\nSelect the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 and 2 only","b":"1, 2 and 3","c":"1 and 3 only","d":"3 only"},"answer":"c","reason":"Rigvedic ashma-chakra and ahava (pail) plus pre-Rigvedic ox-drawn ploughs support both claims; the sickle/axe reference is irrelevant.","confidence":"medium"},{"q":21,"topic":"Current Affairs","stem":"Tungurahua Volcano, which was declared a Global Geopark by UNESCO in 2025, is situated in which one among the following countries?","statements":None,"select_prompt":"","options":{"a":"Ecuador","b":"Peru","c":"Bolivia","d":"Colombia"},"answer":"a","reason":"Tungurahua stratovolcano lies in the Ecuadorian Andes; its surrounding area became a UNESCO Global Geopark in 2025.","confidence":"high"},{"q":22,"topic":"Environment","stem":"With reference to Madhav National Park, which of the following statements is/are correct?","statements":["It was declared a Tiger Reserve in India in 2025.","Sakhya Sagar, which is designated as a Ramsar Site, is situated within this National Park.","Its area is shared between Madhya Pradesh and Rajasthan."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 only","b":"1 and 2","c":"2 and 3","d":"3 only"},"answer":"b","reason":"Madhav NP (Shivpuri, MP) became India's 58th Tiger Reserve in 2025 and contains the Ramsar-listed Sakhya Sagar; it lies entirely in MP.","confidence":"high"},{"q":23,"topic":"Geography","stem":"With reference to the climate of Andaman and Nicobar Islands, which of the following statements is/are correct?","statements":["The climate can be defined as a humid, tropical coastal climate.","It receives rainfall from both South-west monsoon and North-east monsoon.","Maximum precipitation is between December and May."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 only","b":"1 and 2","c":"2 and 3","d":"3 only"},"answer":"b","reason":"Humid tropical coastal climate receiving rainfall from both SW and NE monsoons; maximum precipitation is May-December, not Dec-May.","confidence":"high"},{"q":24,"topic":"Geography","stem":"Which of the following geographical features or phenomena is/are associated with the Peninsular Block of India?","statements":["Submergence of parts of the western coast due to tectonic activity","Presence of residual mountain ranges such as the Veliconda hills and Mahendragiri hills","Deep, V-shaped river valleys formed by fast-flowing rivers"],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 only","b":"1 and 2","c":"2 and 3","d":"3 only"},"answer":"b","reason":"Peninsular Block shows western-coast submergence and residual ranges like Velikonda and Mahendragiri; V-shaped valleys are Himalayan features.","confidence":"medium"},{"q":25,"topic":"Current Affairs","stem":"Consider the following statements with reference to the Sagarmala Programme of the Government of India:","statements":["The Sagarmala Programme seeks to achieve port-led economic growth through cost-effective and sustainable coastal infrastructure.","The success of the Sagarmala Programme is reflected in significant growth in coastal and inland waterway shipping, along with improved global port rankings.","Sagarmala 2.0 aims to position India as a global maritime innovation hub aligned with Atmanirbhar Bharat and Viksit Bharat 2047 visions."],"select_prompt":"Which of the following relationships among the above statements is/are correct?\n1. Statement II validates the effectiveness of the strategies envisioned in statement I.\n2. Statement III extends the objectives of statement I by embedding them into a future-oriented innovation framework.\n3. Statement I contradicts statement III by focusing only on traditional infrastructure instead of modern innovation.\nSelect the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 only","b":"1 and 2","c":"2 and 3","d":"3 only"},"answer":"b","reason":"Sagarmala's growth outcomes validate its strategy (1) and 2.0 extends it via innovation (2); statement III's contradiction claim is wrong.","confidence":"medium"}]

Q26_50 = [{"q":26,"topic":"Environment","stem":"Consider the following statements about Rhynchostylis retusa (Foxtail orchid):","statements":["It is an epiphytic orchid.","The species is endemic to North-east India.","It is the State flower of Arunachal Pradesh and Assam."],"select_prompt":"Which of the statements given above is/are correct?","options":{"a":"1 only","b":"1 and 3","c":"2 and 3","d":"3 only"},"answer":"b","reason":"Foxtail orchid is epiphytic and the State flower of Assam (and Arunachal Pradesh); it is not endemic to NE India.","confidence":"high"},{"q":27,"topic":"Art & Culture","stem":"Which one of the following statements with regard to the Moidams, built by the Tai-Ahom kingdom and inscribed as a World Heritage Site by UNESCO, is/are correct?","statements":["They acted as army fortresses.","They were recreation centres of the Royals and Nobles.","They were burial grounds of the Royals and Nobles.","They were battle drill centres of the Royals and Nobles."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 only","b":"1 and 3","c":"3 only","d":"2 and 4"},"answer":"c","reason":"Moidams of Charaideo are mound-burial tombs of Ahom royals and nobles, inscribed by UNESCO in 2024 as India's 43rd World Heritage Site.","confidence":"high"},{"q":28,"topic":"Environment","stem":"At the United Nations Ocean Conference (UNOC) held in June, 2025 in France, Food and Agricultural Organization (FAO) of the United Nations demonstrated its leading voice on marine and ocean issues, especially on sustainable fisheries and aquaculture for resilient livelihood and 'Blue Transformation'.\nWhich of the following combinations about the 'Four Betters' proposed by FAO for 'Blue Transformation' is correct?","statements":None,"select_prompt":"","options":{"a":"Better production, better nutrition, better environment and better ocean","b":"Better production, better nutrition, better environment and better life","c":"Better coral reefs, better nutrition, better environment and better life","d":"Better estuaries, better nutrition, better environment and better mangrove vegetation"},"answer":"b","reason":"FAO's Strategic Framework Four Betters = better production, better nutrition, better environment, better life.","confidence":"high"},{"q":29,"topic":"Geography","stem":"Which of the following statements with reference to Lake Turkana is/are correct?","statements":["It is the largest desert lake in the world.","The lake is situated in South Sudan along the eastern fringe of the Sahara desert.","The lake is listed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site and is also referred to as the 'Jade Sea'."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 only","b":"1 and 3 only","c":"2 and 3 only","d":"1, 2 and 3"},"answer":"b","reason":"Lake Turkana is the world's largest permanent desert lake (nicknamed 'Jade Sea') and a UNESCO WHS, but it lies in Kenya, not South Sudan.","confidence":"high"},{"q":30,"topic":"Environment","stem":"Which one of the following is the first Plan Vivo certified Reducing Emissions from Deforestation and Forest Degradation (REDD+) project in India?","statements":None,"select_prompt":"","options":{"a":"Uttarakhand REDD+ project","b":"ICFRE-ICIMOD Transboundary REDD+ project in North-Eastern Himalayas","c":"Khasi Hills Community REDD+ project","d":"Sikkim Mamley Kamrang Community REDD+ project"},"answer":"c","reason":"The Khasi Hills Community REDD+ Project in Meghalaya was India's first Plan Vivo-certified REDD+ project.","confidence":"high"},{"q":31,"topic":"Environment","stem":"Consider the following statements with reference to India's response to climate change:","statements":["India's Long-Term Low Emission Development Strategy (LT-LEDS) is a crucial tool for achieving net-zero emissions by 2070.","India's 4th Biennial Update Report (BUR-4) submitted in December, 2024 recorded around 8% decrease in Greenhouse gas emissions in 2020 over 2019.","Climate-resilient development necessarily depends on quick and short-term achievement of emission reduction targets."],"select_prompt":"Which of the following relationships among the above statements is/are correct?\n1. Statement I is empirically supported by statement II.\n2. Statement III contradicts the approach implicit in statement I.\n3. Statement I and statement III together establish the premise of long-term sustainability.\nSelect the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 only","b":"1 and 2","c":"2 and 3","d":"3 only"},"answer":"c","reason":"Statement III contradicts long-term LT-LEDS approach (so 2 correct); I+III don't establish sustainability. II supports I.","confidence":"low"},{"q":32,"topic":"Environment","stem":"With respect to the Western Hoolock Gibbons, which of the following statements is/are correct?","statements":["A Sanctuary in North-east India is home to this ape species listed as Endangered in the International Union for Conservation of Nature (IUCN) Red List.","They have specialized brachiation and can easily swing between trees.","They possess a strong and heavy build like gorillas, yet are remarkably agile tree climbers."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 only","b":"1 and 2","c":"2 and 3","d":"3 only"},"answer":"b","reason":"Hoollongapar Sanctuary (Assam) shelters Hoolock Gibbons (Endangered) which are specialised brachiators; they are slender, not gorilla-like.","confidence":"high"},{"q":33,"topic":"Environment","stem":"Which of the following best explain(s) the rationale for protecting mangrove ecosystems in the context of climate resilience?","statements":["Mangroves reduce tidal energy and store freshwater, making them ideal sites for paddy cultivation in saline estuarine belts.","Their salt-sensitive roots filter seawater, making mangroves key to converting coastal land into freshwater aquaculture zones.","By withstanding tidal surges and offering biomass resources, mangroves function both as natural bio-shields and livelihood bases for rural communities."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 only","b":"1 and 2","c":"2 and 3","d":"3 only"},"answer":"d","reason":"Mangroves are natural bio-shields against tidal surges and provide biomass livelihoods; they don't grow paddy or freshwater aquaculture.","confidence":"high"},{"q":34,"topic":"Geography","stem":"In what way(s) does the Vizhinjam International Seaport represent a structural shift in India's maritime trade and logistics policy?","statements":["By functioning exclusively as a domestic cargo hub to reduce reliance on coastal shipping and eliminate the need for foreign collaborations.","By focusing primarily on passenger cruise tourism and heritage shipping to increase Kerala's profile as a maritime heritage destination.","By leveraging its natural deep draft and strategic location to reduce dependence on foreign trans-shipment ports, enhance revenue retention, and reposition India in regional maritime trade."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 only","b":"1 and 2","c":"2 and 3","d":"3 only"},"answer":"d","reason":"Vizhinjam's natural 20-m draft and proximity to global east-west shipping lanes cut India's dependence on Colombo/Singapore trans-shipment.","confidence":"high"},{"q":35,"topic":"Geography","stem":"Identify the river of the Indian sub-continent on the basis of the following information:","statements":["It has an antecedent drainage system.","It flows through three countries.","It originates in the Tibetan Plateau and is an important river for irrigation.","It does not form distributaries."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer from the following:","options":{"a":"Brahmaputra","b":"Indus","c":"Sutlej","d":"Teesta"},"answer":"b","reason":"Indus has antecedent drainage, originates in Tibet, flows through China, India and Pakistan; description matches Indus best.","confidence":"high"},{"q":36,"topic":"Geography","stem":"Which of the following with reference to Indian States is/are not correct?","statements":["Uttar Pradesh shares its boundary with the highest number of other Indian States.","Rajasthan shares the longest international border among all Indian States.","Sikkim is the only State that shares its boundary with just one other Indian State."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 only","b":"1 and 2","c":"2 and 3","d":"3 only"},"answer":"b","reason":"UP shares borders with 8 states (tied with Assam, not sole highest); India's longest international border is with Bangladesh, not via Rajasthan.","confidence":"high"},{"q":37,"topic":"Environment","stem":"Which of the following statements with regard to the arrival of Amur Falcons at Doyang Lake in Nagaland each year from Mongolia is/are correct?","statements":["It showcases how sustained local conservation efforts can contribute to the arrival and protection of international migratory birds.","It reflects the global success of advanced tracking technologies that guide migratory birds back to their stopover sites.","It confirms that Amur Falcons have adapted to permanent residency in India due to favourable habitat changes."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 only","b":"1 and 2","c":"2 and 3","d":"3 only"},"answer":"a","reason":"Pangti village turned from hunting to conservation, ensuring Amur Falcons return safely; tracking tech doesn't 'guide' them, and they remain migratory.","confidence":"high"},{"q":38,"topic":"Economy","stem":"Which among the following is/are the objective(s) of the Rainfed Area Development (RAD) initiative under the National Mission for Sustainable Agriculture (NMSA)?","statements":["Encouraging monoculture in rainfed areas","Increasing rice cultivation in irrigated regions","Enhancing productivity and minimising climatic risks through Integrated Farming Systems (IFS)"],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 only","b":"1 and 2","c":"2 and 3","d":"3 only"},"answer":"d","reason":"RAD promotes Integrated Farming Systems to enhance productivity and reduce climatic risk; it discourages monoculture and isn't about irrigated rice.","confidence":"high"},{"q":39,"topic":"Current Affairs","stem":"Which of the following is/are the most significant implication(s) of obtaining Oeko-Tex certification for Eri Silk in the global textile industry?","statements":["It allows Indian exporters to compete in high-end markets that prioritise chemical-free products.","It confirms that Eri Silk meets international safety, environmental, and quality standards, enabling its entry into premium eco-conscious markets."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 only","b":"2 only","c":"Both 1 and 2","d":"Neither 1 nor 2"},"answer":"c","reason":"Oeko-Tex certifies textiles free of harmful substances, so Eri Silk gaining it opens both high-end chemical-free and premium eco-conscious export markets.","confidence":"high"},{"q":40,"topic":"Geography","stem":"Ships from which of the following countries have to cross the Strait of Hormuz to reach out to the Indian Ocean?","statements":["Bahrain","Syria","Qatar","Egypt"],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 and 2","b":"1 and 3","c":"2 and 3","d":"3 and 4"},"answer":"b","reason":"Bahrain and Qatar lie inside the Persian Gulf and must transit Hormuz; Syria is Mediterranean, Egypt is on the Red Sea / Suez route.","confidence":"high"},{"q":41,"topic":"IR","stem":"Match List I (INTERPOL Notice) with List II (Description):\nA. Silver Notice - 1. To seek information on unidentified bodies\nB. Blue Notice - 2. To collect additional information about a person's identity, location, or activities in relation to a criminal investigation\nC. Black Notice - 3. To provide warning about a person's criminal activities, where the person is considered to be a possible threat to public safety\nD. Green Notice - 4. To identify and trace criminal assets","statements":None,"select_prompt":"Code:","options":{"a":"A-3 B-1 C-2 D-4","b":"A-3 B-2 C-1 D-4","c":"A-4 B-2 C-1 D-3","d":"A-4 B-1 C-2 D-3"},"answer":"c","reason":"Silver -> assets (4); Blue -> person info (2); Black -> unidentified bodies (1); Green -> public-safety warning (3).","confidence":"high"},{"q":42,"topic":"Environment","stem":"Which of the following statements in relation to NIRANTAR (National Institute for Research and Application of Natural Resources to Transform, Adapt and Build Resilience), a platform of institutions under the Ministry of Environment, Forest and Climate Change, is/are correct?","statements":["Ecosystem Survey and Analysis is a vertical under this platform, the lead institute of which is Botanical Survey of India, Kolkata.","Research and Management of Ecosystem Service is a vertical under this platform, the lead institute of which is Central Zoo Authority, New Delhi.","Capacity Development Support is a vertical under this platform, the lead institute of which is Indian Institute of Forest Management, Bhopal."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1, 2 and 3","b":"1 and 3 only","c":"2 only","d":"3 only"},"answer":"b","reason":"Under NIRANTAR, Ecosystem Survey & Analysis is led by BSI Kolkata and Capacity Development by IIFM Bhopal; Research/Mgmt of Ecosystem Services is not led by Central Zoo Authority.","confidence":"medium"},{"q":43,"topic":"Current Affairs","stem":"The Chancellor of the Federal Republic of Germany visited India in January, 2026. Which of the following is/are not correct in terms of outcomes of this visit?","statements":["Signing of a Memorandum of Understanding between the All India Institute of Ayurveda and the University of Hamburg","Signing of a Memorandum of Understanding on Youth Hockey Development between Hockey India and the German Hockey Federation","Establishment of a bilateral dialogue mechanism on the Indo-Pacific","Opening of an Honorary Consul of Germany in Lucknow"],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"2 and 3","b":"1 and 4","c":"3 and 4","d":"1 only"},"answer":"c","reason":"The Indo-Pacific dialogue mechanism and Lucknow Honorary Consul opening were NOT announced; the Ayurveda-Hamburg and Hockey MoUs were signed.","confidence":"low"},{"q":44,"topic":"Sci-Tech","stem":"Which of the following statements about DHRUV64 is/are correct?","statements":["It is the third chip fabricated under the DIR-V Programme with an overall aim to enable the creation of microprocessors for India.","It is India's first homegrown 1.0 GHz, 64-bit dual-core microprocessor."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 only","b":"2 only","c":"Both 1 and 2","d":"Neither 1 nor 2"},"answer":"b","reason":"DHRUV64 is India's first indigenous 1 GHz 64-bit dual-core RISC-V microprocessor under DIR-V, but not the third chip in the programme.","confidence":"medium"},{"q":45,"topic":"Sci-Tech","stem":"The Bureau of Indian Standard (BIS) recently introduced a national standard to test and assess bomb disposal system. Which of the following statements with regard to this system is/are correct?","statements":["The new standard is known as IS 19445 : 2025.","It will improve interoperability of equipment across agencies.","It was developed by TBRL, DRDO in collaboration with the 30th Central Scientific Research Institute, Russia."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1, 2 and 3","b":"2 and 3 only","c":"1 and 2 only","d":"1 only"},"answer":"c","reason":"IS 19445:2025 was developed indigenously by TBRL-DRDO (no Russian collaboration) and improves interoperability across agencies.","confidence":"medium"},{"q":46,"topic":"Current Affairs","stem":"'X', born in the UK, was conferred the Nobel Prize in 2025. He was a professor in an American university when this prize was announced. Identify 'X':","statements":None,"select_prompt":"","options":{"a":"Michel H. Devoret","b":"Richard Robson","c":"John Clarke","d":"Joel Mokyr"},"answer":"d","reason":"Joel Mokyr (UK-born; Northwestern University) shared the 2025 Economic Sciences Nobel for explaining innovation-driven growth.","confidence":"high"},{"q":47,"topic":"Current Affairs","stem":"Which of the following statements with regard to the Grand Slam Tennis Tournaments is/are correct?","statements":["The tournaments have a shared governance structure establishing the partnership among the four Grand Slam tournaments.","They are open for entry to all internationally ranked tennis players above the age of 14.","There is a limitation on the number of 'Wild Cards' a player may receive to compete in a Grand Slam Tournament."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 and 2 only","b":"2 and 3 only","c":"1 only","d":"1, 2 and 3"},"answer":"b","reason":"Eligibility rules cap entries to internationally ranked players above 14, and Wild Cards per tournament are limited; tournaments are independently governed.","confidence":"medium"},{"q":48,"topic":"Sci-Tech","stem":"Which one of the following pairs of semiconductor plants in India and their locations is not correctly matched?","statements":None,"select_prompt":"(Semiconductor Plant : Location)","options":{"a":"CG Power + Renesas + STARS Microelectronics : Gujarat","b":"Tata Semiconductor Assembly and Test Pvt. Ltd. : Assam","c":"HCL-Foxconn Joint Venture India Chip Ltd. : Madhya Pradesh","d":"SicSem Pvt. Ltd. : Odisha"},"answer":"c","reason":"HCL-Foxconn semiconductor JV is located in Jewar, Uttar Pradesh - not Madhya Pradesh.","confidence":"medium"},{"q":49,"topic":"Sci-Tech","stem":"Which of the following statements with regard to India's indigenous new high resolution weather model, the 'Bharat Forecast System,' is/are correct?","statements":["Its objective is to generate forecasts at the Panchayats cluster level.","It was developed by IIT Delhi."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 only","b":"2 only","c":"Both 1 and 2","d":"Neither 1 nor 2"},"answer":"a","reason":"BFS (6-km resolution) provides forecasts at panchayat-cluster level but was developed by IITM Pune, not IIT Delhi.","confidence":"high"},{"q":50,"topic":"Current Affairs","stem":"Consider the following statements with regard to the film 'Boong':","statements":["The film has recently won the British Academy of Film and Television Arts (BAFTA) Award in the Children's and Family Film category.","The film is directed by Lakshmipriya Devi.","This is the first Indian film to win a BAFTA award in the Children's and Family Film category."],"select_prompt":"Which of the statements given above is/are correct?","options":{"a":"1, 2 and 3","b":"2 and 3 only","c":"1 and 2 only","d":"3 only"},"answer":"c","reason":"'Boong', directed by Manipuri filmmaker Lakshmipriya Devi, won a BAFTA in the Children's & Family category; 'first Indian film' claim is disputed.","confidence":"low"}]

Q51_75 = [{"q":51,"topic":"Sci-Tech","stem":"Which of the following statements regarding the features of blockchain technology are correct?","statements":["Records stored in the database may be made visible to relevant stakeholders without risk of alteration.","Copies of the entire database are stored on multiple computers on a network, syncing within seconds.","Consortium blockchain is a blend of public and private blockchains allowing selective data access.","Mathematical algorithms make it impossible to change or delete any data once recorded and accepted."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 and 3","b":"2 and 4 only","c":"1, 2 and 4","d":"1 and 4 only"},"answer":"c","reason":"Blockchain provides transparent immutable records (1), distributed synced copies (2), and cryptographic immutability (4); statement 3's consortium definition is muddled.","confidence":"high"},{"q":52,"topic":"Economy","stem":"An e-commerce revenue model where the seller has control over pricing but doesn't keep products in stock and instead transfers customer orders and shipment details to a third-party supplier, who then ships the goods directly to the customer, is called:","statements":None,"select_prompt":"","options":{"a":"Dropshipping Model","b":"Affiliate Revenue Model","c":"Transaction Fee Revenue Model","d":"Agency Revenue Model"},"answer":"a","reason":"Dropshipping = seller takes orders but a third-party supplier ships directly to the customer.","confidence":"high"},{"q":53,"topic":"Economy","stem":"Which one of the following correctly represents the three key sub-indices of the Financial Inclusion Index (FI-Index) of the Reserve Bank of India (RBI)?","statements":None,"select_prompt":"","options":{"a":"Credit access, Insurance depth, and Pension coverage","b":"Banking access, GDP contribution, and Financial literacy","c":"Access, Usage, and Quality","d":"Access, Affordability, and Transparency"},"answer":"c","reason":"RBI's FI-Index uses three sub-indices: Access (35%), Usage (45%), and Quality (20%).","confidence":"high"},{"q":54,"topic":"Economy","stem":"Which one of the following best describes the key objective of India's 'Open Network for Digital Commerce' (ONDC) initiative?","statements":None,"select_prompt":"","options":{"a":"To allow government control over all digital commerce transactions","b":"To replace private e-commerce players","c":"To break the dominance of large e-commerce platforms by enabling interoperability across networks","d":"To mandate UPI-based payments for all online transactions"},"answer":"c","reason":"ONDC is an open protocol enabling interoperability across e-commerce networks to break platform monopolies.","confidence":"high"},{"q":55,"topic":"Economy","stem":"Which one of the following statements about Unified Payments Interface (UPI) and Central Bank Digital Currency (Digital Rupee) is not correct?","statements":None,"select_prompt":"","options":{"a":"UPI is a real-time payment system but Digital Rupee is akin to sovereign paper currency.","b":"In case of UPI, settlement for end users happens instantly as the money gets immediately debited or credited but in case of Digital Rupee, there is no settlement as the wallet balance gets transferred to another wallet.","c":"UPI transactions are recorded by banks and reflected in bank statements but in case of Digital Rupee, no data is captured in bank statements as transactions are from one wallet to another.","d":"In both the cases (UPI and Digital Rupee), the liability lies with the users and their respective banks."},"answer":"d","reason":"Digital Rupee is a direct liability of the RBI (sovereign), not of users or banks - so statement (d) is the incorrect one.","confidence":"medium"},{"q":56,"topic":"Economy","stem":"Which of the following statements about Real-World Assets (RWA) Tokenization are correct?","statements":["Tokenization is the process of turning real world assets into digital tokens using blockchain technology.","Tokenization of real world assets offers 24 x 7 access, promoting financial inclusion.","Tokenization of real world assets will allow the access to high growth investment opportunities for individuals in India."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1, 2 and 3","b":"2 and 3 only","c":"1 and 2 only","d":"1 and 3 only"},"answer":"a","reason":"All three are correct: tokenization digitises real assets on blockchain, enables 24x7 fractional access, and opens high-growth opportunities to Indian retail investors.","confidence":"high"},{"q":57,"topic":"Economy","stem":"A bond whose proceeds are used only to finance or refinance a combination of both environmental and social projects is called:","statements":None,"select_prompt":"","options":{"a":"Green Bond","b":"Social Bond","c":"Sustainability Bond","d":"Sovereign Bond"},"answer":"c","reason":"Sustainability Bonds combine both green and social project financing, unlike pure Green or Social bonds.","confidence":"high"},{"q":58,"topic":"Economy","stem":"Which of the following statements about M1xchange's role in Micro, Small & Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) financing is/are correct?","statements":["M1xchange provides collateral based loans to MSMEs.","M1xchange facilitates discounting of invoices and Bills of Exchange for MSMEs.","M1xchange functions as a credit rating agency for MSMEs."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1, 2 and 3","b":"2 only","c":"2 and 3 only","d":"1 only"},"answer":"b","reason":"M1xchange is a TReDS platform that only facilitates invoice/Bills of Exchange discounting; it doesn't lend against collateral or rate credit.","confidence":"high"},{"q":59,"topic":"Economy","stem":"Which one of the following best describes the 'Crowding Out Effect' in the context of fiscal policy?","statements":None,"select_prompt":"","options":{"a":"A situation where private investment increases due to increased Government spending","b":"A situation where Government borrowing leads to higher interest rates, which reduces private investment","c":"A situation where an increase in taxes leads to increased private sector investment","d":"A situation where Government spending has no impact on aggregate demand"},"answer":"b","reason":"Crowding out: government borrowing pushes interest rates up, displacing private sector investment.","confidence":"high"},{"q":60,"topic":"Sci-Tech","stem":"Which of the following statements about Rare Earth Elements (REEs) and Critical Minerals is/are correct?","statements":["Modern technological innovations including Artificial Intelligence, robotics and space exploration extensively utilise Rare Earth Elements (REEs).","China has the highest share in mining of REEs followed by India.","The Government of India launched the National Critical Mineral Mission (NCMM) in 2025 to establish a robust framework for self-reliance in the critical mineral sector.","Rare Earth Elements are a set of 13 metallic elements."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 and 3 only","b":"3 only","c":"1, 3 and 4","d":"1, 2 and 4"},"answer":"a","reason":"AI/robotics/space tech use REEs (1) and NCMM was launched in 2025 (3). REEs are 17 elements (not 13), and India is not the second largest miner.","confidence":"medium"},{"q":61,"topic":"Economy","stem":"Which of the following statements about insurance in aviation sector is/are correct?","statements":["'Aviation Hull Insurance' covers the physical aircraft, including the body, engine, and on-board equipment.","Under the Montreal Convention, adopted in 1999 by over 130 countries, including India, airlines are strictly liable to pay compensation to the family/nominee of every deceased passenger without requiring the family to prove fault."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 only","b":"2 only","c":"Both 1 and 2","d":"Neither 1 nor 2"},"answer":"c","reason":"Hull insurance covers aircraft body/engine/equipment; Montreal Convention (1999) imposes strict airline liability for passenger death.","confidence":"high"},{"q":62,"topic":"Economy","stem":"Which of the following statements about Crowdfunding is/are correct?","statements":["Crowdfunding is solicitation of funds (small amount) from multiple investors through a web-based platform or social networking site for a specific project.","Small and Medium Enterprises (SMEs) are able to raise funds at lower cost of capital without undergoing rigorous procedures."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 only","b":"2 only","c":"Both 1 and 2","d":"Neither 1 nor 2"},"answer":"c","reason":"Crowdfunding pools small sums via online platforms (1) and lets SMEs raise capital cheaply without traditional rigorous procedures (2).","confidence":"high"},{"q":63,"topic":"Economy","stem":"With reference to different Committees in India, consider the following details (Committee - Objective - Organization):","statements":["R.N. Malhotra Committee - Comprehensive reforms of Insurance sector - IRDAI","L.C. Gupta Committee - Roadmap for introduction of derivatives trading in India - SEBI","Urjit R. Patel Committee - Roadmap for reforming bank lending to Housing sector - RBI","Y.H. Malegam Committee - Roadmap for reforms in Microfinance sector - RBI"],"select_prompt":"In which of the above rows are all the details correctly matched?","options":{"a":"2 only","b":"2 and 3","c":"1, 3 and 4","d":"2 and 4"},"answer":"d","reason":"L.C. Gupta (derivatives, SEBI) and Y.H. Malegam (microfinance, RBI) are correct. Urjit Patel dealt with monetary policy, not housing.","confidence":"medium"},{"q":64,"topic":"Economy","stem":"Consider the following statements about the Non-Banking Financial Companies (NBFCs) in India:","statements":["NBFCs cannot accept demand deposits.","All the NBFCs operating in India have to be registered with the RBI.","NBFCs form part of the payment and settlement system and can issue cheque drawn on itself.","Deposit insurance facility of Deposit Insurance and Credit Guarantee Corporation (DICGC) is not available to the depositors of deposit taking NBFCs."],"select_prompt":"Which of the statements given above is/are correct?","options":{"a":"1 and 4","b":"1, 2 and 3","c":"4 only","d":"2, 3 and 4"},"answer":"a","reason":"NBFCs cannot accept demand deposits (1) and DICGC insurance is unavailable to NBFC depositors (4); they aren't part of the payment-settlement system.","confidence":"high"},{"q":65,"topic":"Economy","stem":"Consider the following statements about Multidimensional Poverty Index (MPI):","statements":["MPI is calculated using Alkire-Foster methodology.","MPI calculated by NITI Aayog has a total of twelve indicators.","Maternal Health and Bank Account are common indicators in the MPI of NITI Aayog and MPI of United Nations Development Programme (UNDP)."],"select_prompt":"Which of the statements given above is/are correct?","options":{"a":"1 and 2 only","b":"1, 2 and 3","c":"1 and 3 only","d":"2 only"},"answer":"a","reason":"MPI uses Alkire-Foster methodology (1) and NITI Aayog's National MPI has 12 indicators (2); 'Bank Account' is not in UNDP MPI.","confidence":"high"},{"q":66,"topic":"Sci-Tech","stem":"Which of the following statements with regard to genetic medicine is/are correct?","statements":["Genetic medicines correct/compensate for the faulty genes responsible for disease.","Engineered viruses and lipid nanoparticles are used as carriers of the genetic medicine.","Genetic medicines alter the entire DNA sequence."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 only","b":"2 and 3 only","c":"1 and 2 only","d":"1, 2 and 3"},"answer":"c","reason":"Genetic medicines correct faulty genes (1) and use viral vectors / lipid nanoparticles as carriers (2); they target specific genes, not the entire DNA sequence.","confidence":"high"},{"q":67,"topic":"Sci-Tech","stem":"Which of the following statements with regard to Large Language Models (LLMs) used in machine learning is/are correct?","statements":["LLMs assign probabilities to the next possible words and then pick the one with the highest probability.","LLMs process data through mathematical optimization to minimise prediction errors.","LLMs produce unbiased outputs."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 only","b":"1 and 2 only","c":"2 and 3 only","d":"1, 2 and 3"},"answer":"b","reason":"LLMs assign next-token probabilities (1) and use mathematical optimisation to minimise prediction errors (2); their outputs inherit data biases.","confidence":"high"},{"q":68,"topic":"Sci-Tech","stem":"Which of the following statements with regard to stealth technology is/are correct?","statements":["Stealth objects have a very small radar cross-section and are coated with Radar Absorbing Material.","Stealth objects can be detected using specific frequencies.","Stealth objects are coated with metamaterials to increase the scattering of electromagnetic radiation."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 only","b":"2 and 3 only","c":"1 and 2 only","d":"1, 2 and 3"},"answer":"c","reason":"Stealth platforms minimise radar cross-section using RAM (1) and can be detected by certain low-frequency radars (2); metamaterials REDUCE scattering, not increase it.","confidence":"high"},{"q":69,"topic":"Sci-Tech","stem":"Which of the following statements with regard to Black Boxes used in modern aircrafts is/are correct?","statements":["They carry a beacon emitting red light pulses to facilitate underwater detection.","They record both the cockpit voice and flight data.","Their memory units are made using either stainless steel or titanium."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 only","b":"2 and 3 only","c":"1 and 2 only","d":"1, 2 and 3"},"answer":"b","reason":"Black boxes record cockpit voice and flight data (2) with crash-survivable stainless steel / titanium casings (3); their underwater beacons emit ultrasonic pings, not red light.","confidence":"high"},{"q":70,"topic":"Sci-Tech","stem":"Which of the following statements with regard to Green Hydrogen is/are correct?","statements":["It is decarbonized hydrogen obtained from natural gas reforming combined with carbon capture and storage (CCS).","It is produced using electrolysis of water with electricity generated by renewable energy.","National Green Hydrogen Mission of India aims for abatement of nearly 50 MMT of annual greenhouse gas emissions by 2030."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 only","b":"2 and 3 only","c":"2 only","d":"1, 2 and 3"},"answer":"b","reason":"Green hydrogen is electrolysis of water with renewable electricity (2); NGHM targets ~50 MMT GHG abatement by 2030 (3). Statement 1 describes BLUE hydrogen.","confidence":"high"},{"q":71,"topic":"Sci-Tech","stem":"Consider the following statements with regard to involvement of private entities in India's space programme:","statements":["The Indian National Space Promotion and Authorisation Centre (IN-SPACe) is an autonomous agency formed to facilitate participation of private entities.","Agnikul Cosmos launched the world's first flight using 3D-printed rocket engine.","Skyroot Aerospace has developed liquid fuel for GSLV."],"select_prompt":"Which of the statements given above is/are correct?","options":{"a":"1 only","b":"2 and 3 only","c":"1 and 2 only","d":"1, 2 and 3"},"answer":"c","reason":"IN-SPACe is an autonomous body facilitating private players (1); Agnikul's Agnibaan SOrTeD flew the world's first 3D-printed rocket engine (2). Skyroot has not developed GSLV liquid fuel.","confidence":"high"},{"q":72,"topic":"Sci-Tech","stem":"Which of the following statements with regard to drone swarms is/are correct?","statements":["They use Terahertz band of frequency to communicate with the command centre.","Individual drones in the swarm can communicate with other drones in the swarm.","GPS Spoofing is a commonly used technique to counter drone swarm attack."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 only","b":"2 and 3 only","c":"1 and 2 only","d":"1, 2 and 3"},"answer":"b","reason":"Drones in a swarm communicate with each other (2); GPS spoofing is a counter-drone technique (3). They typically use RF, not Terahertz band, with the command centre.","confidence":"medium"},{"q":73,"topic":"Sci-Tech","stem":"Which of the following statements with regard to GenomeIndia Project is/are correct?","statements":["It is a part of the Human Genome Project.","The project is funded by the Department of Biotechnology (DBT), Government of India.","Its primary aim is to build a catalogue of genetic diversity of the Indian population."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 only","b":"2 and 3 only","c":"1 and 2 only","d":"1, 2 and 3"},"answer":"b","reason":"GenomeIndia is a DBT-funded project (2) aimed at cataloguing genetic diversity of the Indian population (3); it's an independent Indian initiative, not part of the Human Genome Project.","confidence":"high"},{"q":74,"topic":"Sci-Tech","stem":"Which of the following statements with regard to the National Quantum Mission (NQM) is/are correct?","statements":["It aims at developing intermediate-scale quantum computers with 50 - 1000 physical qubits.","Its implementation includes setting up of four Thematic Hubs (T-Hubs) in academic and national R&D institutes across India."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 only","b":"2 only","c":"Both 1 and 2","d":"Neither 1 nor 2"},"answer":"c","reason":"NQM targets quantum computers with 50-1000 physical qubits (1) and sets up four Thematic Hubs in computing, communication, sensing/metrology, and materials/devices (2).","confidence":"high"},{"q":75,"topic":"Sci-Tech","stem":"Which of the following statements with regard to India's Deep Ocean Mission is/are correct?","statements":["It was launched by the Ministry of Ports, Shipping and Waterways, Government of India.","Matsya-6000 has been designed to carry 3 people for deep sea exploration.","Samudrayaan is a project under this mission."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 only","b":"2 and 3 only","c":"1 and 2 only","d":"1, 2 and 3"},"answer":"b","reason":"Matsya-6000 carries 3 humans to 6000-m depth (2) and Samudrayaan is under DOM (3); the Mission is run by the Ministry of Earth Sciences, not Shipping.","confidence":"high"}]

Q76_100 = [{"q":76,"topic":"Ethics","stem":"Mr. X, a senior officer, was overseeing a critical vaccination programme during a pandemic. He found that a private service provider responsible for vaccine distribution was compromising on quality to make profits. Despite immense pressure to manage the issue due to vested interests, he raised his voice based on the principles of public administration which he learnt during various training programmes attended across his career. He reported the issue to the appropriate vigilance authority and halted the contract to ensure citizen welfare.\nWhich one among the following principles of public administration was most strongly demonstrated by Mr. X's actions?","statements":None,"select_prompt":"","options":{"a":"Esprit de corps","b":"Equity","c":"Accountability","d":"Delegation"},"answer":"c","reason":"Reporting wrongdoing to vigilance and halting the contract reflects accountability - answering for actions to safeguard public interest.","confidence":"high"},{"q":77,"topic":"Ethics","stem":"In a multi-ethnic district where both economic competition and historical grievances frequently led to community tensions, a flashpoint has arisen with a Government decision to allocate land for a waste management facility near a tribal hamlet, sparking protests by the tribal community, which claimed that the land was sacred and critical to their cultural identity. At the same time, urban residents and local industries supported the project, citing severe solid waste challenges and health concerns due to lack of a proper disposal site. The conflict has escalated with road blockades, social media campaigns, and allegations of police excesses.\nAs a responsible Government official, you are tasked with resolving the situation through mediation, ensuring a sustainable outcome that balances environmental needs, tribal rights, and urban public health.\nConsider the following statements with reference to the above:","statements":["A successful conflict resolution process must begin with acknowledging the cultural concerns of the protesting tribal community before discussing technical alternatives.","The Government should move ahead with the project without delay to address urban health concerns, which outweigh the sentiments of a small group.","Creating a multi-stakeholder dialogue platform - including tribal leaders, environmental experts, and municipal representatives - to build mutual understanding and help de-escalate tensions.","Conducting an independent Environmental and Social Impact Assessment (ESIA) and sharing findings transparently with both sides to facilitate evidence-based decision-making."],"select_prompt":"Which of the statements given above would contribute to the resolution process?","options":{"a":"1, 3 and 4 only","b":"2, 3 and 4 only","c":"1 and 2 only","d":"1, 2, 3 and 4"},"answer":"a","reason":"Statements 1, 3 and 4 use dialogue, cultural sensitivity and evidence-based mediation; statement 2 dismisses tribal rights and worsens conflict.","confidence":"high"},{"q":78,"topic":"Ethics","stem":"Ms. X is a mid-level civil service official working in the urban development department of a major city. Recently, she was involved in approving a contract for a public infrastructure project - a new community park. During the approval process, she received a piece of confidential information indicating that one of the shortlisted contractors had a history of poor workmanship and allegations of corruption in other cities, though nothing had been legally proven. The Head of the Department, Mr. Y, advised her not to disclose this information to the project committee or the public because it could delay the project and damage the city's reputation. However, Ms. X believed that withholding such information compromised transparency and public trust.\nWhat amongst the following should Ms. X do now?","statements":["Immediately disclose the information to the project committee and the public","Recommend removing the contractor from the shortlist to protect the project's integrity","Propose a 'limited disclosure' to an oversight committee, while keeping the information confidential from the public for the time being"],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 and 2 only","b":"3 only","c":"2 and 3 only","d":"1, 2 and 3"},"answer":"b","reason":"Limited disclosure to an oversight body upholds transparency and due process without defaming a contractor on legally-unproven allegations.","confidence":"high"},{"q":79,"topic":"Polity","stem":"'X' was addressing a seminar on the meaning of the term 'law' as provided under Article 13, Part III of the Constitution of India. 'X' explained that the meaning of the term 'law' in the Constitution of India was very comprehensive. It included ordinances, orders and even rules and regulations. 'Y' pointed out that the term 'law' in Article 13 also included custom or usage having the force of law, to which 'X' was not convinced.\nBased on the above, select the correct conclusion from the options given below:","statements":None,"select_prompt":"","options":{"a":"'X' is correct in the interpretation of law, including the view on non-inclusion of custom.","b":"The view of 'Y' that 'law' included custom is not correct.","c":"The views of both 'X' and 'Y' are correct.","d":"The view of only 'Y' is correct."},"answer":"d","reason":"Article 13(3)(a) expressly INCLUDES custom or usage having the force of law within the definition of 'law', so Y is correct.","confidence":"high"},{"q":80,"topic":"Polity","stem":"Consider the following statements with reference to the Constitution of India:","statements":["There is no Article in the Constitution of India that specifies that the Constitution of India will be officially called the 'Constitution of India'.","There is no Article in the Constitution of India that specifies that the Indian Independence Act, 1947 and the Government of India Act, 1935 stand repealed.","There is no Article in the Constitution of India that mentions 26th January, 1950 as the date of the commencement of the Constitution of India."],"select_prompt":"Which one of the following conclusions based on the above statements is correct?","options":{"a":"All three statements are correct.","b":"There is no correct statement.","c":"There are two correct statements that include statement 3.","d":"There is only one correct statement."},"answer":"d","reason":"Only statement 3 is correct - Article 393 names the Constitution and Article 395 repeals the 1947 and 1935 Acts; no Article fixes 26 January 1950.","confidence":"medium"},{"q":81,"topic":"Governance","stem":"Which of the following statements with regard to the persons with disabilities in India is/are correct?","statements":["The Rights of Persons with Disabilities Act, an Act passed by the Parliament of India in 2018, mandates reservation in education and employment, places a legal duty on Governments to ensure accessibility and non-discrimination.","The Sugamya Bharat Abhiyan focuses on achieving universal accessibility for Persons with Disabilities across three key domains - built infrastructure, transport systems and information and communication technology.","The National Divyangjan Finance and Development Corporation (NDFDC) is a public sector organisation set up by the Ministry of Corporate Affairs as a not-for-profit company to promote entrepreneurship among Persons with Disabilities (PwDs)."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 and 2","b":"2 only","c":"1 and 3","d":"1 only"},"answer":"b","reason":"RPwD Act was passed in 2016 (not 2018); NDFDC is under Ministry of Social Justice (not Corporate Affairs); only the Sugamya Bharat description is correct.","confidence":"high"},{"q":82,"topic":"Polity","stem":"Consider the following statements about the provisions pertaining to the Scheduled Castes and the Scheduled Tribes in India:","statements":["Provisions regarding the administration of the Tribal Areas in the States of Assam, Meghalaya, Tripura and Mizoram are given in the Fifth Schedule of the Constitution of India.","Some tribes of India are entitled to exemption from paying Income Tax on certain incomes.","The Constitution of India provides for reservation of seats in Panchayats for women belonging to the Scheduled Castes and the Scheduled Tribes."],"select_prompt":"Which one of the following conclusions based on the above statements is correct?","options":{"a":"There are two correct statements, that include statement 2.","b":"There are two correct statements, that are statements 1 and 3.","c":"There is only one correct statement.","d":"All three statements are correct."},"answer":"a","reason":"Statements 2 and 3 are correct - Section 10(26) exempts certain tribal incomes; Article 243D reserves Panchayat seats for SC/ST women. Assam/Meghalaya/Tripura/Mizoram are under Sixth Schedule, not Fifth.","confidence":"high"},{"q":83,"topic":"Polity","stem":"Consider the following statements in respect of questions asked by the Members in the Parliament of India:","statements":["Unstarred questions are those to which a Member desires an oral answer in the House.","Starred questions are those to which a Member desires a written answer.","No supplementary question can be asked on an unstarred question."],"select_prompt":"Which one of the following conclusions based on the above statements is correct?","options":{"a":"All the three statements are correct.","b":"There are two correct statements, that include statement 2.","c":"There is only one correct statement.","d":"There is no correct statement."},"answer":"c","reason":"Statements 1 and 2 are reversed (starred = oral, unstarred = written); only statement 3 is correct, as supplementaries follow only starred questions.","confidence":"high"},{"q":84,"topic":"Polity","stem":"Consider the following statements about the Committee on the Welfare of Scheduled Castes and Scheduled Tribes of the Parliament of India:","statements":["Although members of this Committee are elected from both Houses of Parliament, the Chairperson of this Committee is appointed by the Chairman of the Rajya Sabha.","Twenty members are elected by the Rajya Sabha and ten members by the Lok Sabha.","No Minister, except for the Union Minister of Social Justice and Empowerment, is eligible to be a member of this Committee.","Members are elected for a fixed term of two years from the date they enter their office."],"select_prompt":"Which one of the following conclusions based on the above statements is correct?","options":{"a":"There are four correct statements.","b":"There is only one correct statement, that is statement 2.","c":"There are two correct statements, that include statement 1.","d":"There is no correct statement."},"answer":"d","reason":"Chairperson is appointed by the Speaker; composition is 20 LS + 10 RS (statement 2 reverses it); no Minister can be a member; term is one year - all four statements are wrong.","confidence":"medium"},{"q":85,"topic":"Defence","stem":"Consider the following statements about Mission Sudarshan Chakra of India:","statements":["It aims to enhance India's air defence, ballistic missile defence and aerial offensive capabilities.","This Mission is being designed to enhance rapid, precise, and powerful defence responses, reinforcing India's strategic autonomy.","One of the aims of this Mission is to cover all public places of India by an expanded nationwide security shield by 2035."],"select_prompt":"Which of the statements given above is/are correct?","options":{"a":"1, 2 and 3","b":"1 and 2 only","c":"2 and 3 only","d":"1 only"},"answer":"b","reason":"Mission integrates air defence, BMD, and offensive capability for strategic autonomy by 2035 - a military shield, not for 'all public places'.","confidence":"medium"},{"q":86,"topic":"IR","stem":"Consider the following statements about river bridges connecting India with neighbouring countries:","statements":["'Maitri Setu', built over Feni river, connects Ramgarh in India with Sabroom in Bangladesh.","Jhulaghat suspension bridge connects India with Myanmar.","Mechi bridge and its approaches connect Panitanki Bypass in India with Kakarvitta in Nepal."],"select_prompt":"Which of the statements given above is/are correct?","options":{"a":"1 and 2","b":"2 and 3","c":"1 only","d":"3 only"},"answer":"d","reason":"Maitri Setu connects Sabroom (India) with Ramgarh (Bangladesh) - so 1 reverses it; Jhulaghat bridge connects India with Nepal, not Myanmar; only statement 3 is correct.","confidence":"high"},{"q":87,"topic":"Polity","stem":"Which of the following statements about a Zero First Information Report (Zero FIR) under the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita (BNSS), 2023 is/are correct?","statements":["A Zero FIR can be lodged at a police station, even though the place of commission of a cognizable/non-cognizable offence is outside the territorial jurisdiction of that police station.","The Officer-in-Charge of the police station where a Zero FIR has been lodged may, with the permission of the competent authority, initiate a preliminary enquiry.","Under Zero FIR, it is obligatory for the informant to furnish information electronically."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1, 2 and 3","b":"2 and 3 only","c":"1 only","d":"2 only"},"answer":"c","reason":"Zero FIR can be lodged at any police station regardless of jurisdiction; the other statements about preliminary enquiry and obligatory electronic info are not the legal position.","confidence":"low"},{"q":88,"topic":"Governance","stem":"With reference to the organisations under the Government of India, consider the following details (Organisation - Function - Controlling Union Ministry):","statements":["Central Economic Intelligence Bureau (CEIB) - To coordinate between various law enforcement agencies - Ministry of Home Affairs","Serious Fraud Investigation Office (SFIO) - To investigate complex corporate frauds - Ministry of Finance","Central Bureau of Investigation (CBI) - To preserve values in public life and ensure the health of the national economy - Ministry of Personnel, Public Grievances and Pension"],"select_prompt":"In how many of the above rows are the given details correctly matched?","options":{"a":"1","b":"2","c":"3","d":"None"},"answer":"a","reason":"Only one row matches - CEIB is under Finance (not Home Affairs); SFIO is under Ministry of Corporate Affairs (not Finance); CBI's described function is wrong (that's CVC).","confidence":"low"},{"q":89,"topic":"IR","stem":"Which of the following international conventions have not been ratified by India?","statements":["Employment Policy Convention","Abolition of Forced Labour Convention","International Convention on the Protection of the Rights of All Migrant Workers and Members of Their Families","Geneva Convention Relative to the Protection of Civilian Persons in Time of War","Convention on Reduction of Statelessness"],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"2 and 4","b":"1 and 2","c":"3 and 4 only","d":"3, 4 and 5"},"answer":"d","reason":"India has ratified ILO 122 and 105 plus 1949 Geneva Conventions; it has not ratified the Migrant Workers Convention or the Statelessness Convention.","confidence":"low"},{"q":90,"topic":"Current Affairs","stem":"Consider the following statements with respect to the AI Impact Summit, 2026 held in New Delhi:","statements":["The Summit's intellectual framework was based on three foundational Sutras: People, Planning, and Progress.","The Preamble of the Summit stresses Democratising AI Resources, which acknowledges the Charter for Democratic Diffusion of AI as a binding framework to support locally relevant innovation and strengthen resilient AI ecosystems while respecting national laws.","The New Delhi Declaration on AI Impact was structured around seven Chakras (Pillars), which included Access for Social Empowerment, AI for Science, and Secure and Trusted AI."],"select_prompt":"Which of the statements given above is/are correct?","options":{"a":"1, 2 and 3","b":"1 and 2 only","c":"2 and 3 only","d":"3 only"},"answer":"d","reason":"Only the seven Chakras pillar structure is correct; the Sutras were People, Planet and Progress, and the Charter is non-binding.","confidence":"medium"},{"q":91,"topic":"IR","stem":"Which of the following connectivity projects is/are a part of cooperation between India and the ASEAN member countries?","statements":["Kaladan Multi-Modal Transit Transport Project","IMT Trilateral Highway","Agartala-Akhaura Rail Line"],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 and 2","b":"2 and 3","c":"1 and 3","d":"2 only"},"answer":"a","reason":"Kaladan (India-Myanmar) and IMT Trilateral Highway (India-Myanmar-Thailand) involve ASEAN states; Agartala-Akhaura links Bangladesh, not in ASEAN.","confidence":"high"},{"q":92,"topic":"IR","stem":"Match List I (Project Supported by India) with List II (Country):\nA. Mangdechhu Hydroelectric Project    1. Maldives\nB. Restoration of Stor Palace          2. Afghanistan\nC. District Hospital at Dickoya        3. Bhutan\nD. Institute of Security and Law Enforcement Studies    4. Sri Lanka","statements":None,"select_prompt":"Code:","options":{"a":"A-1 B-4 C-2 D-3","b":"A-3 B-2 C-4 D-1","c":"A-3 B-4 C-2 D-1","d":"A-1 B-2 C-4 D-3"},"answer":"b","reason":"Mangdechhu - Bhutan(3); Stor Palace - Afghanistan(2); Dickoya Hospital - Sri Lanka(4); Inst. of Security & Law Enforcement - Maldives(1).","confidence":"high"},{"q":93,"topic":"Defence","stem":"Which of the following items of defence hardware is/are manufactured in India?","statements":["Su-30 MKI Fighter Jets","T-90 MK-III Tanks","Akula Class Submarine"],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 and 2","b":"1 and 3","c":"1 only","d":"2 only"},"answer":"a","reason":"Su-30MKI is licence-built by HAL and T-90 tanks are assembled at Avadi; Akula-class submarines are leased from Russia, not manufactured in India.","confidence":"high"},{"q":94,"topic":"IR","stem":"Consider the following statements about platforms for multilateral co-operation:","statements":["The 'Colombo Process' is a regional consultative process in which member states take binding decisions by consensus.","The 'Abu Dhabi Dialogue' is a voluntary non-binding consultative process among Asian countries of labour origin and destination to facilitate regional cooperation on contractual labour mobility.","The 'Global Forum for Migration and Development', created upon the proposal of a former UN Secretary General, is a voluntary forum whose decisions are non-binding in nature."],"select_prompt":"Which of the statements given above is/are correct?","options":{"a":"1, 2 and 3","b":"1 and 3 only","c":"2 and 3 only","d":"2 only"},"answer":"c","reason":"Colombo Process is non-binding and consultative (so 1 is wrong); Abu Dhabi Dialogue and GFMD are correctly described as voluntary non-binding forums.","confidence":"high"},{"q":95,"topic":"IR","stem":"Consider the following UN organisations/agencies:","statements":["World Food Programme","United Nations Children's Fund","United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees","International Labour Organisation"],"select_prompt":"How many of the above has/have been awarded the Nobel Prize twice?","options":{"a":"1","b":"2","c":"3","d":"4"},"answer":"a","reason":"Only UNHCR has won the Nobel Peace Prize twice (1954, 1981); WFP, UNICEF and ILO have each won it once.","confidence":"high"},{"q":96,"topic":"IR","stem":"Match List I (UN Peacekeeping Operation) with List II (Period of Operation):\nA. UNMIL          1. 2007 - 2010\nB. MINURCAT       2. 2002 - 2005\nC. MINUSTAH       3. 2003 - 2018\nD. UNMISET        4. 2004 - 2017","statements":None,"select_prompt":"Code:","options":{"a":"A-3 B-4 C-1 D-2","b":"A-3 B-1 C-4 D-2","c":"A-2 B-1 C-4 D-3","d":"A-2 B-4 C-1 D-3"},"answer":"b","reason":"UNMIL: 2003-2018 (3); MINURCAT: 2007-2010 (1); MINUSTAH: 2004-2017 (4); UNMISET: 2002-2005 (2).","confidence":"medium"},{"q":97,"topic":"IR","stem":"Match List I (BIMSTEC Centre/Establishment) with List II (Location):\nA. BIMSTEC Cultural Industries Observatory    1. NOIDA\nB. BIMSTEC Energy Centre                      2. Bengaluru\nC. BIMSTEC Centre for Weather and Climate     3. Colombo\nD. BIMSTEC Technology Transfer Facility       4. Thimphu","statements":None,"select_prompt":"Code:","options":{"a":"A-3 B-2 C-1 D-4","b":"A-3 B-1 C-2 D-4","c":"A-4 B-2 C-1 D-3","d":"A-4 B-1 C-2 D-3"},"answer":"c","reason":"Cultural Industries Observatory - Thimphu (4); Energy Centre - Bengaluru (2); Weather & Climate - NOIDA (1); Tech Transfer Facility - Colombo (3).","confidence":"low"},{"q":98,"topic":"Defence","stem":"Which one of the following pairs (Indian Army Corps : Headquarters) is not correctly matched?","statements":None,"select_prompt":"","options":{"a":"3 Corps : Dimapur","b":"4 Corps : Tezpur","c":"14 Corps : Leh","d":"33 Corps : Srinagar"},"answer":"d","reason":"33 Corps HQ is at Sukna (West Bengal), not Srinagar; Srinagar hosts 15 Corps.","confidence":"high"},{"q":99,"topic":"Governance","stem":"Which of the following statements with respect to the Revamped Rashtriya Gram Swaraj Abhiyan (RGSA) is/are correct?","statements":["The period of its implementation is 1st April, 2021 to 31st March, 2026.","The key objective of the Revamped RGSA is to develop the governance capabilities of the Panchayati Raj Institutions to deliver on the Sustainable Development Goals.","The share of the Central funding for the Revamped RGSA is 100% for all States and Union Territories."],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1 and 2","b":"2 only","c":"1 and 3","d":"2 and 3"},"answer":"a","reason":"Revamped RGSA period is 2021-22 to 2025-26 (statement 1 correct); aim is to build PRI capabilities for SDGs (2). Funding is 60:40 / 90:10 - not 100%.","confidence":"medium"},{"q":100,"topic":"IR","stem":"Which of the following countries are members of the European Union?","statements":["Belarus","Poland","Germany","Switzerland"],"select_prompt":"Select the answer using the code given below:","options":{"a":"1, 2 and 4","b":"1 and 4 only","c":"2 and 3","d":"2 and 4 only"},"answer":"c","reason":"Only Poland and Germany are EU members; Belarus and Switzerland are not.","confidence":"high"}]


